⚡️🇺🇸 The USS Enterprise (CVN-65), the first ever Nuclear Powered Aircraft Carrier that served the US Navy from 1961-2017 (58yrs) had officially been certifiably cleared of all nuclear components last week, and today, all 95,000t of the Big E were beginning their final trek from Newport News, VA to Mobile Bay, Alabama where the remainder of the ship will be scrapped.

A portion of the USS Enterprise lives on in it’s namesake successor, the USS Enterprise (CVN-80), the third Gerald R. Ford-class Supercarrier as a chunk of steel in the keel of the carrier.

